# 64_group_by_two_keys_ordered
# The correct multi-key shape, kept beside the three refusals so that tightening the
# projection rule cannot be mistaken for narrowing the fragment: two grouping columns, both
# projected, one aggregate after them, ordered by that aggregate and limited. This is the
# shape `select acct, cur, sum(amt) … group by acct, cur` takes in `gbs.niles` and in the
# benchmark, and it must keep serving.
2 200 20 x1
3 null 30 x1
